{"results":[{"url":"https://www.congress.gov/nomination/116th-congress/2252","final_url":"https://www.congress.gov/nomination/116th-congress/2252","title":"PN2252 - Nomination of Amy Coney Barrett for Supreme Court of the United States, 116th Congress (2019-2020)","description":"PN2252 - Nomination of Amy Coney Barrett by the U.S. President for Associate Justice of the Supreme Court of the United States at Supreme Court of the United States, 116th Congress (2019-2020)","language":"en","text":"Citation\n\n Subscribe\n\n Share/Save\n\n Site Feedback\n\n# PN2252 — Amy Coney Barrett — Supreme Court of the United States 116th Congress (2019-2020)\n\n## Nomination\n\nHide Overview\n\n## Description\n\n* Amy Coney Barrett, of Indiana, to be an Associate Justice of the Supreme Court of the United States, vice Ruth Bader Ginsburg, deceased.\n\n## Organization\n\n* Supreme Court of the United States\n\n## Latest Action\n\n* 10/26/2020 - Confirmed by the Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 52 - 48. Record Vote Number: 224.\n\n## Date Received from President\n\n* 09/29/2020\n\n## Committee\n\n* Senate Judiciary\n\n## Actions: PN2252 — 116th Congress (2019-2020)\n\n| Date | Senate Actions |\n| --- | --- |\n| 10/26/2020 | Confirmed by the Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 52 - 48. Record Vote Number: 224. |\n| 10/25/2020 | Cloture invoked in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 51 - 48. Record Vote Number: 222. |\n| 10/23/2020 | Motion by Senator Schumer to recommit to Senate Committee on the Judiciary tabled in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 53 - 44. Record Vote Number: 219. |\n| 10/23/2020 | Motion by Senator Schumer to indefinitely postpone tabled in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 53 - 44. Record Vote Number: 218. |\n| 10/23/2020 | Cloture motion presented in Senate. |\n| 10/23/2020 | Motion to proceed to executive session to consideration of nomination agreed to in Senate by Yea-Nay Vote. 51 - 46. Record Vote Number: 217. |\n| 10/22/2020 | Placed on Senate Executive Calendar. Calendar No. 890. |\n| 10/22/2020 | Reported by Senator Graham, Committee on the Judiciary, without printed report. |\n| 10/22/2020 | Committee on the Judiciary. Ordered to be reported favorably. |\n| 10/15/2020 | Committee on the Judiciary. Hearings held. Hearings printed: S.Hrg. 116-637. |\n| 10/14/2020 | Committee on the Judiciary. Hearings held. Hearings printed: S.Hrg. 116-637. |\n| 10/13/2020 | Committee on the Judiciary. Hearings held. Hearings printed: S.Hrg. 116-637. |\n| 10/12/2020 | Committee on the Judiciary. Hearings held. Hearings printed: S.Hrg. 116-637. |\n| 09/29/2020 | Received in the Senate and referred to the Committee on the Judiciary. |","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":8072.432748998835,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}